s/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-om.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-21T16:05:19.524871+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-om.1--plan","local_name":"bob-cli-om.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-om","agent_clan_generation":"20261121103321","agent_session":"bob-cli-om.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"bob-cli-om.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-om[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Wikilink completion in Bob's prose prompts[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Typing `[[` in any Bob-owned field that writes Markdown prose into [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the vault (intentions, Work/Rotten/Cancel/Schedule Log reasons, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]record text, notebook summaries, the Mac Pull-In reason) opens one [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]consistent LINK band that inserts exactly the link it shows, never [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]submits a half-typed link, never touches text after the caret, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]never writes the vault. Identifier and filter fields stay literal.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]prose_wikilink_completion.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/prose_wikilink_completion.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-om[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-om/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix bob's wikilink field range and ranking, publish shared [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]vectors[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-link-fixes[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-link-fixes: in bob-cli, end unclosed link fields at the caret, keep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]authored #subpath and |alias text when the target is replaced, break [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ranking ties by depth then inbound links, publish [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests/fixtures/wikilink_complete/vectors.json, and write the new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decisions strand.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian link engine (field model, ranking port, metadata [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]index)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]link-engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-link-fixes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]link-engine: in bob-navigation-hotkeys, add pure JS fragments for the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]field model and ranking that replay bob's vectors exactly, plus a lazy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]LinkIndex built on Obsidian's metadataCache. No UI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]proseField controller, LINK band, and the Work summary pilot[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]link-band[dim] · [dim][/dim]after link-engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]link-band: build the two-mode proseField controller and the LINK band [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](rendering, CSS, keyboard contract, undo-safe insertion, a11y, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unresolved-link hint) and api.proseField v1. Pilot it on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]block-id-prompt's Work summary prompt (S1) and verify undo, IME, and Esc[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]layering in real Obsidian.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Standalone modal prompts[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]modal-prompts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after link-band[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal-prompts: opt surfaces S2-S6, S12, and S13 into links with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]correct sourcePath. Keep each host's guards, and close the Ctrl+[ gaps [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on these surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task Card stages and the scheduled inline reason[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]task-card-prompts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after link-band[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-card-prompts: opt the Task Card picker stages S7-S10 into links [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the shared picker wiring. Add S11, the scheduled-stage reason [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tail, through minOffset so the date token never completes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Intention Card fields[/bold #D7AFFF]                                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]intention-card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after link-band[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]intention-card: attach proseField to the Intention Card's intention [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]input, summary input, and reflection textarea (S14). The band must [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]survive repaints and [ / ] travel, and it is the first rung of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]card's back-out ladder.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Record Card typed stages and link-stage convergence[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]record-card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after link-band[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]record-card: attach proseField to the Record Card's text, suggest, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list stages (S15). Converge the link stage onto the engine in field [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mode, retiring recordCardLinkCandidates and its bracket bug, and survive[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the per-keystroke repaint.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob capture-complete --links-only[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-links-only[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-link-fixes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-links-only: add -L/--links-only and -S/--source-note to bob [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-complete. They complete only wikilink fields in plain prose and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]never apply capture grammar. Includes help, docs-gen, and tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac Pull-In reason link band[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-pull-in[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-links-only[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-pull-in: wire the Pull-In cancel reason field (S16) in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-mac-capture to capture-complete --links-only. Render a LINK band in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the recall band's slot with the same key contract, fail open on an older[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob, and watch macOS CI to green.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prose-field role lint and end-to-end walkthrough[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-lint[dim] · [dim][/dim]after modal-prompts, task-card-prompts, intention-card, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]record-card[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-lint: mark every text control in bob-plugins with a role (prose, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]literal, mixed, or none) and add a contract test that pins the S1-S15 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]allowlist and its wiring. Then run one isolated real-Obsidian [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]walkthrough across representative surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-om","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli"